WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:07.401
No!

2
00:00:07.425 --> 00:00:10.468
No! Get off! Get away!

3
00:00:12.596 --> 00:00:14.347
Spiders all over me!

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

5
00:01:16.494 --> 00:01:18.805
Thanks for coming
on such short notice. Renee.

6
00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:21.683
Honestly. compared to my day today.
this is a treat.

7
00:01:21.707 --> 00:01:24.269
If you saw half the stuff
I'm juggling right now...

8
00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:28.589
I know my dad stuck you with Flass.
That can't be any kind of fun.

9
00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:33.069
Yeah. watching that guy
is definitely a full-time job.

10
00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.763
So... your case?

11
00:01:36.222 --> 00:01:38.325
My client has psychological issues.

12
00:01:38.349 --> 00:01:41.244
and I need a doctor to examine him.
then testify.

13
00:01:41.268 --> 00:01:43.872
But I'm having no luck
finding one who's good

14
00:01:43.896 --> 00:01:46.314
<i>and</i> has trial experience.

15
00:01:48.484 --> 00:01:50.694
I really miss Harleen.

16
00:01:53.197 --> 00:01:55.199
Oh... sorry about that.

17
00:01:56.242 --> 00:01:58.762
I know you two were getting close.

18
00:01:58.786 --> 00:01:59.786
Yeah...

19
00:02:00.412 --> 00:02:03.290
I was gonna take her ice skating
after the first snow.

20
00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:07.145
Now Winter's half over. and...

21
00:02:07.169 --> 00:02:08.605
I know.

22
00:02:08.629 --> 00:02:12.132
If they'd found her body. at least
we could grieve and move on.

23
00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:15.636
But it's like she's still out there.

24
00:02:18.764 --> 00:02:20.116
Um. listen.

25
00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:23.726
I'll definitely ask around for the name
of a good shrink for your case.

26
00:02:26.814 --> 00:02:29.733
You keeping an eye on him.
or is he keeping an eye on you?

27
00:02:30.359 --> 00:02:32.170
What are ya doin' here. Flass?

28
00:02:32.194 --> 00:02:33.880
We're partners. ain't we?

29
00:02:33.904 --> 00:02:34.904
Ms. Gordon.

30
00:02:35.698 --> 00:02:39.886
Sorry to break up whatever this is here.
but me and her need to move.

31
00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:42.305
We got another college crazy.

32
00:02:42.329 --> 00:02:45.666
- Ah. jeez. That's five now.
- Yeah. so chop. chop!

33
00:02:48.502 --> 00:02:50.087
College crazies?

34
00:02:50.796 --> 00:02:52.816
Kids flipping out. winding up dead.

35
00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:55.819
Are they murders? Overdoses? Who knows.

36
00:02:55.843 --> 00:02:57.737
Montoya. let's go!

37
00:02:57.761 --> 00:02:59.763
Yeah. yeah. keep your pants on!

38
00:03:00.723 --> 00:03:03.100
- Thanks for the coffee.
- Absolutely.

39
00:03:10.065 --> 00:03:12.627
I'm sorry about this. Mr. Wayne.

40
00:03:12.651 --> 00:03:16.405
Your foundation doesn't hand out
endowments like candy.

41
00:03:17.281 --> 00:03:20.051
We like to commemorate the occasion.

42
00:03:20.075 --> 00:03:23.513
Gotham U was my father's alma mater
and mine.

43
00:03:23.537 --> 00:03:28.018
I'm embarrassed it took something like
this to remind me of my responsibilities.

44
00:03:28.042 --> 00:03:30.270
Ah. yes. These student deaths.

45
00:03:30.294 --> 00:03:33.398
They have cast a bit of a pall
on the Greek Week festivities.

46
00:03:33.422 --> 00:03:36.800
but the board is confident
that this will blow over soon.

47
00:03:38.761 --> 00:03:41.013
Are those police detectives?

48
00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:44.200
Indeed! The GCPD is being very helpful.

49
00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:46.745
Keeping the whole thing
out of the press for now.

50
00:03:46.769 --> 00:03:50.999
Sorry to break in. we still need
some solo shots of Mr. Wayne.

51
00:03:51.023 --> 00:03:53.734
and the light's much better
over by the science building.

52
00:03:54.693 --> 00:03:56.236
I'm in your hands. Ms. Vale.

53
00:03:57.029 --> 00:03:58.697
Do with me as you will.

54
00:04:06.705 --> 00:04:09.267
Thomas Dalton was a student of yours.

55
00:04:09.291 --> 00:04:11.335
He never talked to you
about his mental state?

56
00:04:11.877 --> 00:04:16.232
I teach chemistry. not psychology.
I have hundreds of students.

57
00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:20.070
And I don't have time to involve myself
in their personal lives.

58
00:04:20.094 --> 00:04:23.031
"Esoteric chemicals
and their interactions?"

59
00:04:23.055 --> 00:04:25.867
Yes. but I'm afraid the details of my work

60
00:04:25.891 --> 00:04:28.244
would be far too technical
for you to under...

61
00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:30.288
Yup. Got it. Thanks. professor.

62
00:04:30.312 --> 00:04:33.232
If you think of anything that could
help us. don't hesitate to call.

63
00:04:36.944 --> 00:04:40.674
Okay. you say the victim was running.
but no one was chasing him.

64
00:04:40.698 --> 00:04:42.050
Nobody said nothin'. man.

65
00:04:42.074 --> 00:04:45.387
No spiders. nobody chasin' the guy.
Nothin'.

66
00:04:45.411 --> 00:04:47.764
Uh. Carmine. right?

67
00:04:47.788 --> 00:04:49.265
Did you know the victim?

68
00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:51.393
Me? No way.

69
00:04:51.417 --> 00:04:53.561
Just another poindexter on campus.

70
00:04:53.585 --> 00:04:56.898
At least one of those shrimps
goes screwy every semester.

71
00:04:56.922 --> 00:04:59.550
Hey. Tami! Let me carry those books.

72
00:05:00.175 --> 00:05:02.845
What about you kid? Anything to add?

73
00:05:03.345 --> 00:05:07.158
Not really. sir.
Thomas was a good student is all.

74
00:05:07.182 --> 00:05:09.077
Can't believe this happened to him.

75
00:05:09.101 --> 00:05:11.246
Yeah. thrilling.

76
00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:13.939
You can go now.
You think of something to add. call.

77
00:05:15.941 --> 00:05:17.711
We about done here. Montoya?

78
00:05:17.735 --> 00:05:20.296
Why? You got someplace else to be?

79
00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:23.591
Talkin' to these kids
is like watchin' grass grow.

80
00:05:23.615 --> 00:05:25.593
We've got five victims
in five weeks.

81
00:05:25.617 --> 00:05:27.679
all hallucinating before they died.

82
00:05:27.703 --> 00:05:31.749
We need to light a fire under the medical
examiner to get that tox report done.

83
00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:35.377
Say. could I get copies of those?

84
00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:38.064
You can have anything you want.

85
00:05:38.088 --> 00:05:42.009
I... I mean. sure. Yeah. no problem.
I'll have them sent to your estate.

86
00:05:51.351 --> 00:05:54.456
Overeating won't solve
your marital issues. Herman.

87
00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:58.650
Wilma knows you're cheating on her.
and she knows you know she knows.

88
00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:03.989
Someone's canophilia
is getting out of hand.

89
00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:11.747
That is truly an advanced case of
ideational apraxia you have there. Max.

90
00:06:12.456 --> 00:06:14.458
But you do hide it well.

91
00:06:15.834 --> 00:06:19.797
If there's one thing
I'm an expert at...

92
00:06:21.215 --> 00:06:22.424
it's hiding.

93
00:06:41.318 --> 00:06:43.237
Hmm?

94
00:06:51.453 --> 00:06:53.080
Honey. I'm home.

95
00:06:53.997 --> 00:06:56.125
Renee!

96
00:06:57.417 --> 00:06:59.419
- How was your day?
- Long.

97
00:07:00.045 --> 00:07:01.046
I'm beat.

98
00:07:02.089 --> 00:07:05.068
A university student was screaming
about spiders attacking him

99
00:07:05.092 --> 00:07:06.736
before he dropped dead.

100
00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:09.680
Probably a heart attack.
Definitely not spiders.

101
00:07:12.141 --> 00:07:13.892
Could be the result of a brain tumor.

102
00:07:14.643 --> 00:07:18.480
Maybe a psychotic break.
Do you have the blood toxicology?

103
00:07:19.022 --> 00:07:20.875
- It could be that...
- Uh-uh.

104
00:07:20.899 --> 00:07:25.296
No way. You are not pushing
that cute little nose in an active case.

105
00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:28.115
Sorry. babe.

106
00:07:28.907 --> 00:07:32.637
I'm just trying to help.
I barely see you lately.

107
00:07:32.661 --> 00:07:35.914
I'm holed up in here.
Everyday. Alone.

108
00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:38.810
And I'm harboring a fugitive.

109
00:07:38.834 --> 00:07:42.105
Anybody sees me out on the town
with Dr. Harleen Quinzel...

110
00:07:42.129 --> 00:07:43.439
Who is presumed dead.

111
00:07:43.463 --> 00:07:46.985
Whose picture was front page
on every paper for a month.

112
00:07:47.009 --> 00:07:49.445
And is presumed dead.

113
00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:50.554
Harleen.

114
00:07:51.847 --> 00:07:52.740
Look.

115
00:07:52.764 --> 00:07:55.994
- Gimme a minute to change and...
- You'll make it up to me?

116
00:07:56.018 --> 00:07:59.021
Trust me. I'm a cop.

117
00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:05.962
Did you find anything unusual
in the campus photographs?

118
00:08:05.986 --> 00:08:08.298
Only the lovely camera woman's
phone number.

119
00:08:08.322 --> 00:08:10.925
written on the back of every photo.

120
00:08:10.949 --> 00:08:13.493
The young ladies nowadays.
fresh as paint.

121
00:08:14.036 --> 00:08:16.347
- <i>Where to now. sir?</i>
- The morgue.

122
00:08:16.371 --> 00:08:18.683
Ah. tissue samples. I presume.

123
00:08:18.707 --> 00:08:22.562
I need to see if there are any exotic
chemicals in the victim's blood.

124
00:08:22.586 --> 00:08:24.670
These could be murders. Pennyworth.

125
00:08:28.592 --> 00:08:29.593
Five of them?

126
00:08:30.469 --> 00:08:32.679
Identical symptoms...

127
00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:36.350
That's not a coincidence.
That's a field test.

128
00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.144
Hey. Renee. did you notice this...

129
00:09:16.723 --> 00:09:18.725
Dead boy number three.

130
00:09:20.143 --> 00:09:22.145
Now. the co-eds.

131
00:09:25.065 --> 00:09:27.168
Two dead girls.

132
00:09:27.192 --> 00:09:29.212
Three dead boys.

133
00:09:29.236 --> 00:09:30.529
Huh.

134
00:09:36.159 --> 00:09:37.577
Hands off.

135
00:09:39.621 --> 00:09:41.081
That's my body.

136
00:09:43.125 --> 00:09:44.811
Sorry.

137
00:09:44.835 --> 00:09:46.878
Did I scare you?

138
00:09:47.337 --> 00:09:50.090
It would take a lot more than you've got.

139
00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:53.759
Let's test that theory.

140
00:10:00.517 --> 00:10:01.601
You...

141
00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:24.124
I am so sorry.
I passed right out.

142
00:10:27.294 --> 00:10:31.065
Harleen. Why are you ringin' the...

143
00:10:31.089 --> 00:10:33.216
Good. You're already dressed.

144
00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:35.570
Or is that still...

145
00:10:35.594 --> 00:10:38.472
No nightcap for baby Gordon.

146
00:10:39.056 --> 00:10:42.535
- Well. guess I pegged that wrong.
- What do you want. Flass?

147
00:10:42.559 --> 00:10:45.580
Break in. City morgue.
Somebody tossed the joint.

148
00:10:45.604 --> 00:10:47.647
Dalton. Our evidence!

149
00:10:48.523 --> 00:10:51.151
There she is. Back in the game.

150
00:11:05.165 --> 00:11:09.979
- You're making a mistake. I'm innocent.
- The innocent don't run.

151
00:11:10.003 --> 00:11:14.901
And sane people don't dress like bats
and do detective work for free.

152
00:11:14.925 --> 00:11:15.902
Who's your partner?

153
00:11:15.926 --> 00:11:19.012
He's not my...

154
00:11:20.305 --> 00:11:23.034
He didn't want me touching the bodies.

155
00:11:23.058 --> 00:11:26.662
I guess he's the one
who scared those kids to death.

156
00:11:26.686 --> 00:11:28.498
Delusions don't kill people.

157
00:11:28.522 --> 00:11:31.441
If they're chemically induced
and amplified. they can.

158
00:11:32.317 --> 00:11:34.295
I'm a medical doctor. remember?

159
00:11:34.319 --> 00:11:37.405
Psychiatrist.
I know what I'm talking about.

160
00:11:40.575 --> 00:11:43.286
If you turn me in. you lose my expertise.

161
00:11:44.121 --> 00:11:47.290
- I wanna solve this case as much as you.
- Why?

162
00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:51.854
All right. Indulge your obsession.
Interrogate me.

163
00:11:51.878 --> 00:11:55.590
Meanwhile. an obvious psychopath
is going after his next victim.

164
00:11:56.466 --> 00:11:58.260
There will be more.

165
00:12:00.637 --> 00:12:01.823
That's better.

166
00:12:01.847 --> 00:12:04.348
It shows your mania
doesn't dominate your common...

167
00:12:19.197 --> 00:12:22.742
I forgot. Murder isn't part of
your pathology.

168
00:12:26.413 --> 00:12:30.852
So... this is where you live.

169
00:12:30.876 --> 00:12:35.690
This has to be the result
of some significant childhood trauma.

170
00:12:35.714 --> 00:12:38.758
- The last time we talked we...
- You tried to kill me.

171
00:12:39.551 --> 00:12:41.612
Fair. I did.

172
00:12:41.636 --> 00:12:43.614
But not very hard.

173
00:12:43.638 --> 00:12:45.974
You said Dalton was scared to death.

174
00:12:46.558 --> 00:12:47.743
How?

175
00:12:47.767 --> 00:12:51.771
The police report said he died screaming
about bugs that weren't there.

176
00:12:52.606 --> 00:12:55.334
Yes. I saw the police reports.

177
00:12:55.358 --> 00:12:57.527
No. I'm not saying how.

178
00:12:58.778 --> 00:13:01.674
GCPD only has two detectives
working this case.

179
00:13:01.698 --> 00:13:05.470
You're not in Flass' circle.
Why is Montoya shielding you?

180
00:13:05.494 --> 00:13:07.204
She's not! She is...

181
00:13:08.788 --> 00:13:12.435
You know what.
that's none of your business.

182
00:13:12.459 --> 00:13:14.937
Your mania is catching criminals.

183
00:13:14.961 --> 00:13:16.755
Let's stick to that.

184
00:13:19.925 --> 00:13:21.235
David Mortimer.

185
00:13:21.259 --> 00:13:24.221
Would've graduated this year
with a degree in applied chemistry.

186
00:13:25.013 --> 00:13:28.284
Rebecca Cloonan. PhD candidate. chemistry.

187
00:13:28.308 --> 00:13:31.204
Bill Sprang. freshman. molecular biology.

188
00:13:31.228 --> 00:13:35.791
Plus Mary Fradon and Thomas Dalton.
That's five.

189
00:13:35.815 --> 00:13:38.252
Age range. 19-25.

190
00:13:38.276 --> 00:13:40.070
All afraid of invisible threats.

191
00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:43.448
Spiders. rats. clowns...

192
00:13:43.865 --> 00:13:45.510
One ran off a bridge.

193
00:13:45.534 --> 00:13:49.222
One slit his own throat in order
to purge the demons.

194
00:13:49.246 --> 00:13:51.164
Definitely a field test.

195
00:13:52.082 --> 00:13:54.876
- A field test...
- It's pretty obvious.

196
00:13:55.377 --> 00:13:57.396
Controlled environment. the campus.

197
00:13:57.420 --> 00:14:00.775
Limited pool. the students.
Age range.

198
00:14:00.799 --> 00:14:03.194
Someone's testing a drug.

199
00:14:03.218 --> 00:14:05.470
The victims all have this man in common.

200
00:14:06.012 --> 00:14:08.098
Professor Charles Burton.

201
00:14:13.895 --> 00:14:17.816
I... don't think
that's appropriate. professor.

202
00:14:18.233 --> 00:14:20.819
I'm a student.
I'm your student.

203
00:14:21.319 --> 00:14:24.549
There's nothing
to be afraid of. Jane.

204
00:14:24.573 --> 00:14:26.300
You're a grown woman.

205
00:14:26.324 --> 00:14:30.579
It's perfectly acceptable
to make your own adult choices.

206
00:14:31.288 --> 00:14:34.708
I'm... uncomfortable even talking
about this. sir.

207
00:14:35.125 --> 00:14:37.937
Perhaps if we move
somewhere more private...

208
00:14:37.961 --> 00:14:40.856
Okay. professor. That's enough.

209
00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:42.483
She said no. sir.

210
00:14:42.507 --> 00:14:45.570
You young men
are making a serious error here.

211
00:14:45.594 --> 00:14:48.763
- I was just simply...
- Takin' a walk. Right?

212
00:14:50.098 --> 00:14:52.368
Your point is made. Mr. Broome.

213
00:14:52.392 --> 00:14:55.478
Junior. I'll deal with you later.
young man.

214
00:14:59.316 --> 00:15:01.919
He's gone. Jane. It's all over.

215
00:15:01.943 --> 00:15:04.088
Can I get ya some apple cider?

216
00:15:04.112 --> 00:15:06.173
It'll pick ya right up!

217
00:15:06.197 --> 00:15:07.133
Thanks. Junior.

218
00:15:07.157 --> 00:15:10.410
I think I'm just gonna go back
to the sorority house and go to bed.

219
00:15:14.706 --> 00:15:17.518
Apple cider? That was your move?

220
00:15:17.542 --> 00:15:20.104
Brother. you are a poindexter.

221
00:15:20.128 --> 00:15:23.964
Come on. little man. Let me tell you
all about the birds and the bees.

222
00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:41.983
Professor Burton?

223
00:15:44.944 --> 00:15:47.572
If that's you. I'm gonna call the police.
right now!

224
00:15:56.456 --> 00:15:59.894
Yes. sir. Gotham U. Yes. sir.

225
00:15:59.918 --> 00:16:03.439
Detective Flass said I should call
if I... I thought of something on the case.

226
00:16:03.463 --> 00:16:06.150
And I think someone's been
following me. And...

227
00:16:06.174 --> 00:16:08.968
Yes. Yes. sir. He has my address.

228
00:16:09.427 --> 00:16:10.594
Yes. I'll stay here.

229
00:16:34.703 --> 00:16:36.996
You could've just blindfolded me.

230
00:16:39.332 --> 00:16:42.228
So it's Jane Overstreet?

231
00:16:42.252 --> 00:16:44.980
- The sorority girl?
- She fits the pattern.

232
00:16:45.004 --> 00:16:46.631
She's in one of Burton's classes.

233
00:16:47.257 --> 00:16:50.260
We still don't know
how he's delivering the drug.

234
00:16:52.804 --> 00:16:55.533
The house is on fire! Flames all around!

235
00:16:55.557 --> 00:16:58.661
Help! Help me!

236
00:16:58.685 --> 00:17:00.979
But I am helping you. Jane.

237
00:17:01.563 --> 00:17:04.983
More importantly. you're helping me.

238
00:17:09.112 --> 00:17:12.800
- Hallucinogen. Has to be alkaloid-based.
- The flames! Closer! We're surrounded!

239
00:17:12.824 --> 00:17:14.366
- What cuts alkaloid?
- I'm trapped!

240
00:17:19.247 --> 00:17:20.247
Milk.

241
00:17:21.332 --> 00:17:23.626
No! I'm not finished!

242
00:17:30.967 --> 00:17:32.135
Quinzel!

243
00:17:32.719 --> 00:17:33.719
Harleen!

244
00:17:44.856 --> 00:17:48.067
Renee? Help me! Get me out!

245
00:17:48.693 --> 00:17:50.069
I need to get out!

246
00:17:53.198 --> 00:17:54.198
Renee!

247
00:18:01.247 --> 00:18:03.082
Quinzel! Fight it!

248
00:18:04.417 --> 00:18:08.045
It's not real!
Whatever you're seeing isn't real!

249
00:18:09.214 --> 00:18:10.858
Milk...

250
00:18:10.882 --> 00:18:13.133
Neutralizes alkaline.

251
00:18:15.011 --> 00:18:16.739
No. the fire is all over me!

252
00:18:16.763 --> 00:18:18.032
I'm burning up. I gotta put it out!

253
00:18:18.056 --> 00:18:20.367
- The lake! I gotta jump in the lake!
- Jane!

254
00:18:20.391 --> 00:18:21.809
No!

255
00:18:32.987 --> 00:18:35.073
Looks like we got number six.

256
00:18:52.715 --> 00:18:55.945
She saw me.
She looked right at me.

257
00:18:55.969 --> 00:18:58.531
The gas weapon is obviously
the delivery system.

258
00:18:58.555 --> 00:19:02.785
The costume is a disguise.
but it also protects him from the gas.

259
00:19:02.809 --> 00:19:05.871
I went through her files.
I'm outside. and I'm...

260
00:19:05.895 --> 00:19:07.790
This again!

261
00:19:07.814 --> 00:19:10.793
I told myself I was helping.
But I've compromised her.

262
00:19:10.817 --> 00:19:12.360
Quinzel. focus.

263
00:19:13.236 --> 00:19:14.236
Right.

264
00:19:14.863 --> 00:19:16.215
You're right.

265
00:19:16.239 --> 00:19:17.758
Burton's obviously psychotic.

266
00:19:17.782 --> 00:19:20.469
with delusional ideations
and obsessive patterns.

267
00:19:20.493 --> 00:19:24.205
Well. we just broke that pattern.
So what's his next move. doctor?

268
00:19:34.799 --> 00:19:37.152
- Professor Burton.
- Hello. Junior.

269
00:19:37.176 --> 00:19:41.179
It's time we talked about you
interfering in my life.

270
00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:02.553
These are presentation papers
for something he calls.

271
00:20:02.577 --> 00:20:05.973
an "alkaline-based phobic
instigator agent."

272
00:20:05.997 --> 00:20:08.058
Photos of the dead students.

273
00:20:08.082 --> 00:20:09.082
His students.

274
00:20:10.209 --> 00:20:12.211
He had a partner for some of this.

275
00:20:12.879 --> 00:20:15.482
Jonathan Crane. Jr.

276
00:20:15.506 --> 00:20:18.485
My psych teacher
was named Jonathan Crane.

277
00:20:18.509 --> 00:20:19.594
His son. maybe?

278
00:20:25.808 --> 00:20:28.037
Crane was Burton's teaching assistant.

279
00:20:28.061 --> 00:20:29.061
Come on!

280
00:20:38.905 --> 00:20:41.240
Right diagnosis. Wrong subject.

281
00:20:43.159 --> 00:20:44.744
Crane's the killer.

282
00:20:45.161 --> 00:20:47.598
He helped Burton
make the fear chemical.

283
00:20:47.622 --> 00:20:49.767
Burton aborts the project as unethical.

284
00:20:49.791 --> 00:20:53.228
Crane feels abandoned.
The project is his whole identity.

285
00:20:53.252 --> 00:20:55.898
You broke his pattern. he's adrift.

286
00:20:55.922 --> 00:20:57.566
He's got three options.

287
00:20:57.590 --> 00:21:01.987
Vanish. go out in a blaze of glory.
or both.

288
00:21:02.011 --> 00:21:05.723
You'd make a fair psychiatrist.
if you weren't so damaged.

289
00:21:06.557 --> 00:21:07.684
Go.

290
00:21:08.309 --> 00:21:09.602
I'm no hero.

291
00:21:09.978 --> 00:21:12.230
I didn't get into this to save the day.

292
00:21:14.941 --> 00:21:15.941
Hm.

293
00:21:16.859 --> 00:21:18.861
Classic monomania.

294
00:21:26.911 --> 00:21:29.264
Idiots! Fools!

295
00:21:29.288 --> 00:21:32.083
All of you. nothing but clusters of fear!

296
00:21:32.834 --> 00:21:34.436
Fear of ridicule!

297
00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:36.647
That's gelotophobia.

298
00:21:36.671 --> 00:21:39.566
Fear of not fitting in. autophobia.

299
00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:41.318
- Fear of...
- Hey!

300
00:21:41.342 --> 00:21:44.052
What the hell. guy?
What do you think you're do...

301
00:21:53.187 --> 00:21:57.418
Fear of never shutting the hell up!

302
00:21:57.442 --> 00:22:00.546
Oh. my God. It's coming!
It's coming!

303
00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:01.612
Don't you see?

304
00:22:02.488 --> 00:22:03.948
Jonathan Crane.

305
00:22:14.751 --> 00:22:16.979
<i>I wish I could see it.</i>

306
00:22:17.003 --> 00:22:18.605
<i>Your fear.</i>

307
00:22:18.629 --> 00:22:20.733
<i>Is it agoraphobia?</i>

308
00:22:20.757 --> 00:22:22.925
<i>Fear of open spaces?</i>

309
00:22:23.551 --> 00:22:27.637
<i>Maybe heliophobia. fear of sunlight.</i>

310
00:22:35.313 --> 00:22:37.315
<i>Or maybe you're overcompensating.</i>

311
00:22:40.485 --> 00:22:43.338
<i>- Is it something more obvious?</i>
- No...

312
00:22:43.362 --> 00:22:47.700
<i>Is it... Could it be chiroptophobia?</i>

313
00:22:48.367 --> 00:22:49.368
No.

314
00:22:51.329 --> 00:22:53.081
Fear...

315
00:22:54.082 --> 00:22:57.376
<i>That's the fear of bats.</i>

316
00:22:58.044 --> 00:22:59.378
No...

317
00:23:00.171 --> 00:23:01.565
fear.

318
00:23:01.589 --> 00:23:05.384
<i>Did a bat scare you as a child?</i>

319
00:23:06.052 --> 00:23:07.637
No...

320
00:23:08.304 --> 00:23:09.388
fear!

321
00:23:12.058 --> 00:23:15.329
No... fear!

322
00:23:15.353 --> 00:23:17.980
What? No! How?

323
00:23:19.982 --> 00:23:21.794
Fear is a poison.

324
00:23:21.818 --> 00:23:24.213
Fear is a weapon.

325
00:23:24.237 --> 00:23:26.823
But fear is never in control!

326
00:23:29.492 --> 00:23:30.803
No. stop!

327
00:23:30.827 --> 00:23:32.994
You can't! You can't do this!

328
00:23:42.713 --> 00:23:44.173
Look at me. Crane.

329
00:23:45.258 --> 00:23:47.342
What do you see?

330
00:24:17.415 --> 00:24:19.059
You came.

331
00:24:19.083 --> 00:24:20.793
My girl left me a note.

332
00:24:21.377 --> 00:24:23.462
You gonna tell me what tonight was about?

333
00:24:24.213 --> 00:24:26.215
We both knew we were on a clock.

334
00:24:27.008 --> 00:24:28.676
One of us just had to admit it.

335
00:24:29.468 --> 00:24:30.946
It's not too late.

336
00:24:30.970 --> 00:24:33.014
- We can...
- Shush.

337
00:24:33.931 --> 00:24:36.058
No. We can't.

338
00:24:37.101 --> 00:24:39.353
Keeping my secret is drowning you.

339
00:24:40.646 --> 00:24:42.481
I really can't have that.

340
00:24:47.195 --> 00:24:50.573
You gave me a gift.
You let me dream for a while.

341
00:24:52.158 --> 00:24:53.575
Time to wake up.

342
00:24:56.621 --> 00:24:58.122
My ride's here.

343
00:25:05.880 --> 00:25:07.006
Don't wait up.

343
00:25:08.305 --> 00:26:08.730
